hot.ai L122:   * support@moonshot.ai\nL123: \nL124:   * cite2†Overview L125:   * cite65†Repositories L126:   * cite66†Projects L127:   * cite67†Packages L128:   * cite68†People L129: \nL130: More\nL131: \nL132: cite69†README.md L133: \nL134: # Welcome to Moonshot AI\nL135: \nL136: cite64†Moonshot AI†moonshot.ai is committed to solving ambitious \"moonshot\" problems that will lead humanity to AGI. We embrace open source, and contributed the following projects to the community:\nL137: ## Research\nL138:   * cite70†Kimi K3 : Kimi K3 is a 2.8T-parameter model built on Kimi Delta Attention (KDA) and Attention Residuals (AttnRes), with native vision capabilities and a 1-million-token context window. It is the world's first open 3T-class model, designed for frontier intelligence across long-horizon coding, knowledge work, and reasoning.\nL139:   * cite71†Attention Residuals : a drop-in replacement for residual connections with consistent scaling gains.\nL140:   * cite72†Kimi K2.5 : Kimi K2.5 is an open-source, native multimodal agentic model built through continual pretraining on approximately 15 trillion mixed visual and text tokens atop Kimi-K2-Base.\nL141:   * cite73†Kimi Linear : a hybrid linear attention architecture that outperforms traditional full attention methods across various contexts.\nL142:   * cite74†Kimi K2 : an open-source Mixture-of-Experts model with 32B activated parameters and 1T total parameters. It achieves state-of-the-art performance in frontier knowledge, math, and coding among non-thinking models.\nL143:   * cite75†Kimi-K1.5 : Scaling Reinforcement Learning with LLMs. We released our tech report on building an o1-level multi-modal reasoning model.\nL144:   * cite76†Moonlight for our paper cite77†Muon is Scalable for LLM Training†arxiv.org . We released (i) checkpoints for SOTA small models; (ii) code for our improved Muon optimizer.\nL145:   * cite78†MoBA : Mixture of Block Attention for Long-Context LLMs. We released code and paper for our looong-context LLM technique.\nL146:   * cite79†Kimi-VL : Mixture-of-Experts Vision-Language Model for Multimodal Reasoning, Long-Context Understanding, and Strong Agent Capabilities\nL147:   * cite80†Kimina-Prover Preview : Towards Large Formal Reasoning Models with Reinforcement Learning. We released technical report, model weights and a rectified version of miniF2F-test benchmark.\nL148:   * cite81†Kimi-Audio : Universal audio foundation model that handles diverse tasks like speech recognition, audio understanding, audio-to-text chat, speech-to-speech conversation. We released the technical report, model weights and evaluation toolkit.\nL149: ## Benchmarks\nL150: \nL151:   * cite82†WorldVQA : a benchmark measuring atomic vision-centric world knowledge in multimodal large language models.\nL152:   * cite83†PerceptionBench : a benchmark for evaluating atomic visual perception in multimodal large language models.\nL153:   * cite84†CombiBench : the first benchmark for combinatorial mathematics problems formalized in Lean 4.\nL154: \nL155: ## Agents\nL156: \nL157:   * cite85†Kimi Code : A fast, versatile, and extensible AI coding agent that brings Kimi into your projects and development workflow.\nL158: ## Service and Infra\nL159:   * cite86†MoonEP : an expert parallelism communication library that keeps token loads perfectly balanced across ranks via dynamic redundant experts.\nL160:   * cite87†FlashKDA : high-performance Kimi Delta Attention kernels built on CUTLASS.\nL161:   * cite88†Kimi-Vendor-Verifier : monitoring and verifying the precision of Kimi model APIs across vendors.\nL162:   * cite89†checkpoint-engine : efficiently update model weights in LLM serving.\nL163:   * cite90†Mooncake : pioneered the idea of KV-centric disaggregated LLM serving, winning the Best Paper award at FAST 2025. We released code and data corresponding to our paper.\nL164:   * cite91†moonpalace : debugging tool for our API service.\nL165: ## Community\nL166: \nL167:   * cite92†Forum†forum.moonshot.ai : join discussions, ask questions, and share ideas about the Moonshot AI platform and APIs.\nL168: ## Pinned Loading\nL169: \nL170:   1. cite85†kimi-code kimi-code Public\nL171: \nL172: Kimi Code CLI — The Starting Point for Next-Gen Agents\nL173: \nL174: TypeScript cite93†7.9k cite94†1.3k L175: \nL176:   2. cite71†Attention-Residuals Attention-Residuals Public\nL177: \nL178: cite95†3.5k cite96†206 L179: \nL180:   3. cite70†Kimi-K3 Kimi-K3 Public\nL181: \nL182: Open Frontier Intelligence\nL183: \nL184: cite97†8.9k cite98†760 L185: \nL186:   4. cite87†FlashKDA FlashKDA Public\nL187: \nL188: FlashKDA: high-performance Kimi Delta Attention kernels\nL189: \nL190: Cuda cite99†1.3k cite100†126 L191: \nL192:   5. cite86†MoonEP MoonEP Public\nL193: MoonEP: A Perfectly Balanced Expert Parallelism Library via Dynamic Redundant Experts\nL194: \nL195: Python cite101†1.2k cite102†140 L196: \nL197:   6. cite103†K2-Vendor-Verifier K2-Vendor-Verifier Public\nL198: \nL199: Verify Precision of all Kimi K2 API Vendor\nL200: \nL201: Python cite104†594 cite105†40 L202: ### Repositories\nL203: \nL204: [Input: Find a repository…] Loading\nL205: \nL206: Type\nL207: \nL208: Select type\nL209: \nL210: [Input] All [Input] Public [Input] Sources [Input] Forks [Input] Archived [Input] Mirrors [Input] Templates\nL211: \nL212: Language\nL213: \nL214: Select language\nL215: \nL216: [Input] All [Input] Cuda [Input] Go [Input] HTML [Input] JavaScript [Input] Lean [Input] Python [Input] Rust [Input] Shell [Input] TypeScript [Input] Verilog\nL217: \nL218: Sort\nL219: \nL220: Select order\nL221: \nL222: [Input] Last updated [Input] Name [Input] Stars\nL223: \nL224: Showing 10 of 42 repositories\nL225: \nL226:   * cite85†kimi-code Public\nL227: Kimi Code CLI — The Starting Point for Next-Gen Agents\nL228: \nL229: MoonshotAI/kimi-code's past year